<title>USA: FSA qualifies eight muni bond issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies eight muni bond issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>FSA said Wednesday it qualified for bond insurance the following eight municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Dartmouth, Mass., $4.04 million general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Mississippi, $111 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Albany County, N.Y., $28.7 million public improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Albany County, N.Y., $9.418 million public improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Babylon Union Free School District, N.Y., $6.34 million school bonds.</p>
<p>--Dallas, Texas, $62 million water and sewer bonds.</p>
<p>--Texas Southern University, Texas, $15.09 million improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Wisconsin, $115.2 million GOs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
